            <ArticleTitle>[Tolerance to standard and non-ionic contrast media in patients with ischemic heart disease and stable angina pectoris during coronary angiography].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>35-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Angiography of the coronary arteries with iohexol was carried out in 45 coronary patients with stable angina pectoris and that with diatrizoate in another group of 45 similar patients. Iohexol was tolerated better that diatrizoate. Physiological and hemodynamic side effects of iohexol were less marked than those of diatrizoate.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
